query:
Define a modified kernel
\begin{equation}\label{eq:K1def}
K_1(t)\equiv |t|\,K_0(t)=\frac{|t|}{2\sinh(|t|/2)},
\end{equation}
and the corresponding operator
\[
(\mathcal{K}_1 f)(\rho)\equiv \int d\rho'\;K_1(\rho-\rho')\big(f(\rho')-f(\rho)\big).
\]
Show that $\phi_\nu$ is still an eigenfunction and that its eigenvalue is
\begin{equation}\label{eq:chi1_second_derivative}
\chi_1(\nu)\equiv \chi_{K_1}(\nu)= -\frac{d^2}{d\nu^2}\chi_0(\nu).
\end{equation}
